@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy & storage"; }
<article class="shell policy-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE TRANSPARENCY</p><h1>Privacy &amp; storage.</h1>
    <p>Your shopping bag is saved in this browser. It contains product identifiers and quantities, and remains on this device until you empty your bag or clear your browser?s site data.</p>
    <p>Guest checkout requires your name, email and delivery address. When you place an order, these details and the purchased products are stored on the server. No account or payment details are required, and no payment is collected.</p>
    <p>While an order submission is awaiting confirmation, this tab temporarily saves its contact, address and bag details so you can safely retry after a connection failure. These temporary details are removed after confirmation or when the browser tab session ends.</p>
    <p>Your order confirmation link is private. Anyone with the link can view your order and delivery details, so share it only with people you trust.</p>
    <p>Product images are hosted locally. Image source and license information is included in the project?s image credits file.</p>
    <a class="text-link" asp-action="Cart">Manage your bag</a>
</article>
